# What Prettier must not rewrite.
#
# This file is the ONLY place the formatter's scope is narrowed. Both
# `npm run format` (writer) and `npm run format:check` (gate) run against `.`,
# so they describe one set by construction.
#
# Before this file existed they did not. `format` wrote `.` while `format:check`
# checked a hand-maintained allowlist glob, so `npm run format` rewrote ~100
# files the gate had never inspected. A formatter whose writer and checker
# disagree will silently reformat whatever falls in the gap; that is how a
# 53-file sweep landed unannounced on 2026-08-06.
#
# Prettier already skips `node_modules`, `.git`, and everything in `.gitignore`
# (so `dist/`, `coverage/`, `.vite/`, `.venv*/` need no entry here). Only add a
# path below when automatic formatting would actively damage it, and say why.

# --- Hand-wrapped prose -----------------------------------------------------
# Line breaks in these are authorial. Prettier's markdown printer reflows
# paragraphs and renormalises tables, which destroys deliberate structure in the
# design spine, worklogs, and dated addenda — documents whose diffs are read as
# a historical record.
*.md
docs/

# --- Externally owned or machine-generated ----------------------------------
# npm owns this; Prettier has no legitimate opinion about it.
package-lock.json

# The img2threejs forge writes these (sculpt specs, camera configs, generated
# TS factories, review HTML). Reformatting them makes the next tool run produce
# a spurious diff against its own output.
assets/workbench/

# --- Captured evidence ------------------------------------------------------
# Acceptance and audit output. These are records of what a run emitted;
# rewriting them edits the evidence.
artifacts/
.playwright-mcp/

# --- Tool and editor state --------------------------------------------------
# Machine-written configuration, not source.
.agent/
.claude/
.commandcode/
.openai/
.wrangler/

# --- Separate workspace -----------------------------------------------------
# Has its own package.json, tsconfig, and verification chain
# (`npm run test:kernel-probe`). Formatting is that workspace's call.
experiments/
